":[\\\"s-decl-recovery\\\",\\\"s-decl-prepare-reply\\\",\\\"s-recovery-init\\\",\\\"s-prepare-reply-adopt\\\",\\\"s-subcase-dispatch\\\",\\\"s-preaccept-reply\\\"],\n  \\\"scope\\\": {\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Variant of the value-adoption harness that first lets the instance owner commit the value X and then fail, so that the same instance is recovered by a replica that holds no command while another live replica holds X committed. Sequence: replica 1's conflicting premise; owner replica 0 proposes X on (0,0); replica 1's non-equal pre-accept reply is delivered and replica 1 then fails; replica 2's reply makes the owner enter the Accept phase at ballot 0 towards replicas 2 and 3, of which replica 3 never pre-accepted the command; both AcceptReplies are delivered, so the owner COMMITS X (status COMMITTED) and broadcasts Commit - the harness delivers that Commit only to replica 2 (the first live peer in the owner's preferred order) and then fails the owner; replica 3 then runs startRecoveryForInstance(0,0) and the quiescent exchange is completed.\\\",\n   \\\"assumptions\\\":[\n    \\\"Same construction, row sizing, transport boundary and crash model as the value-adoption experiment (in-process replicas, marshaled RPC structs decoded per delivery, FIFO per link, no delivery to crashed replicas).\\\",\n    \\\"The owner's Commit reaching only replica 2 models the owner failing immediately after the first Commit of its broadcast, which is a permitted crash point.\\\",\n    \\\"No production logic is modified; the authority and crash flags are set only through the target's own fields and handlers.\\\"\n   ],\n   \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No client path, no state-machine execution, no run() loop or recovery timer loop in the harness.\\\"],\n   \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"n\\\":5,\\\"f\\\":2,\\\"owner\\\":0,\\\"recoverer\\\":3,\\\"committed_peer\\\":2,\\\"value_ballot\\\":0,\\\"recovery_ballot\\\":8}\n  },\n  \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"The harness drives the package's own startPhase1/bcastPreAccept/handlePreAcceptReply/bcastAccept/handleAcceptReply path for the owner's commit, delivers the owner's Commit to replica 2 only, fails the owner, then calls startRecoveryForInstance(0,0) at replica 3 and delivers the resulting Prepare/PrepareReply and PreAccept traffic through the target's own handlers, recording each replica's instance state before and after.\\\",\n  \\\"requirement\\\":\\\"A recovery of an instance that a peer reports as COMMITTED must not replace that value, and the recovering leader's phase-1 proposal must still be able to reach its quorum.\\\",\n  \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"The recovering coordinator's adoption of a reply's Status into lb.status together with the guard that discards later replies (epaxos/epaxos.go:847-895) and its value adoption rule (epaxos/epaxos.go:1236-1313); the peer's report of COMMITTED is the target's own honest reply.\\\",\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\": [\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"owner-committed-value\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"instance_state\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replica\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"phase\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"after_commit\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":4},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"cmd_op\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}]},\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"live-peer-committed-value\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"instance_state\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replica\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":2},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"phase\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"after_commit\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":4},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"cmd_op\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}]},\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"recovery-start\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"recovery_start\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replica\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"self_has_command\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"self_status\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"self_vballot\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":8}]},\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"committed-reply\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"prepare_reply\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replica\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":2},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":4},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"has_command\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"cmd_op\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}]}\n  ],\n  \\\"comparisons\\\": [\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"recovery_proposal\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"replica\\\",\\\"instance_row\\\",\\\"instance_index\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"recovery-start\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"cmd_op\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},\n    \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"quorum_reply_command_op\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}],\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"The value the recovery proposes does not replace the value the quorum reports; violated when the recovery's PreAccept carries the NOOP (cmd_op 0) although a reply carried X with status COMMITTED.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"instance_state\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"replica\\\",\\\"instance_row\\\",\\\"instance_index\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"recovery-start\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":4},\n    \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"phase\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"final\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replica\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3}],\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"The recovering replica's own instance reaches a decided state after the recovered proposal; violated when it remains in a pre-accept state because the adopted COMMITTED status made the leader discard the replies it needed.\\\"}\n  ]\n }\n}\njson.dump(u,open('draft/update9.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ntimeout 120 /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_15-11-32-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission update9.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"written\n{\"valid\": true, \"run_id\": \"73a2daf4c12b4b32aa4abd9f7c66b640\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 1358.2800980159955, \"diagnostics\": [], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\", \"no_change\": false, \"execution_requested\": true, \"effects\": [{\"object\": \"sources\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"s-preaccept-reply\"}, {\"object\": \"knowledge\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"@k-preaccept-reply-status-guard\"}, {\"object\": \"investigations\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"@rec-status-guard-stall\"}, {\"object\": \"experiments\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"experiment\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update9.json\",\"summary\":\"Requested execution of a sharper variant probe and recorded a second mechanism it exposed locally. In the new scenario the owner commits X and fails after its Commit reaches only one live peer, so replica 2 holds X COMMITTED while replica 3 recovers the same instance holding no command. Local native feedback shows the recovery proposing the NOOP although replica 2's prepare reply carried X with status COMMITTED, and then stalling: adopting that COMMITTED status into lb.status makes the guard at epaxos/epaxos.go:870 discard replica 4's reply, so the restarted phase-1 proposal never reaches its fast quorum and replica 3's instance stays pre-accepted with no accept or commit emitted. That mechanism is recorded as a new behavior with a new source range (epaxos/epaxos.go:847-895) and a new active question about whether the stall repeats identically on the executor's retry, with the two comparisons (recovery proposes the quorum-reported value; the recovering replica reaches a decided state) declared for the controller's receipt. This turn's unfinished work: the interpretation of that receipt and confirmation that the observed incompleteness is the target's status-guard interaction rather than harness scheduling.\"}"}}
